{"id": "unknown-2026-08-21-007", "date": "2026-08-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Air bubbles boost cooling and hydrogen production in photovoltaic-thermal system", "content": "<p>Researchers in India developed a PVT-hydrogen system using air-bubble injection to improve cooling, thermal and electrical efficiency, and hydrogen production. Tested outdoors in Tamil Nadu, the system achieved a peak thermal efficiency of 45.5% and hydrogen production of 15.5 ml/min.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/air-bubbles-boost-cooling-and-hydrogen-production-in-photovoltaic-thermal-system/\">Air bubbles boost cooling and hydrogen production in photovoltai", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/air-bubbles-boost-cooling-and-hydrogen-production-in-photovoltaic-thermal-system/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-21-008", "date": "2026-08-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh mandates solar charging for millions of electric rickshaws", "content": "<p>Bangladesh plans to require millions of battery-powered auto-rickshaws to use solar-powered charging stations as a condition of registration, aiming to reduce pressure on the electricity grid. Industry representatives say the policy could spur investment in solar charging infrastructure, create jobs and expand renewable energy, while urging the government to include net metering.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/bangladesh-mandates-solar-charging-for-millions-of", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/bangladesh-mandates-solar-charging-for-millions-of-electric-rickshaws/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-21-009", "date": "2026-08-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Report alleges U.S. solar recycling is mostly landfilling, offshoring in disguise", "content": "<p>A new white paper from Sustainable Source Studios cites regulatory filings, industry disclosures and IEA lifecycle datasets in concluding that most U.S. solar module recycling yields degraded, landfilled, or offshored material.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/bombshell-report-alleges-u-s-solar-recycling-is-mostly-landfilling-offshoring-in-disguise/\">Report alleges U.S. solar recycling is mostly landfilling, offshoring in disguise</a> appeared first on <a href=\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/bombshell-report-alleges-u-s-solar-recycling-is-mostly-landfilling-offshoring-in-disguise/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-21-010", "date": "2026-08-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar powerhouse to storage leader", "content": "<p>Chile is transforming in a bid to avoid becoming a victim of its own solar success. Developers have flooded the Atacama Desert with solar projects, turning Chile into a PV powerhouse but also drastically reducing revenues and driving some operators into bankruptcy. S&#38;P Global Energy’s Ángel Cancino sees the country increasingly focusing on energy storage to rescue some of its overbuilt PV capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/solar-powerhouse-to-storage", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/21/solar-powerhouse-to-storage-leader/", "type": "rss"}]}
